   {
    "id": "a1",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "Body: 1-junction of the lunar module. Inertia = modulated spatial I (m(t), J(m)); Out1..6 = MR, r = -dm/dt and -dJ/dt: the propellant that leaves takes its momentum with it.",
    "x": 400,
    "y": 60,
    "w": 560,
    "h": 60
   },
   {
    "id": "a2",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "Landing gear: four footpads (167.57 in from the X axis, TN D-6850), each a ContactPoint (Hunt-Crossley normal force for pad, strut and soil; Coulomb friction mu = 0.4) on the lunar sphere below it (LunarSurface3D), mounted at its pad through a FixedTransform3DNeutral.",
    "x": 1000,
    "y": 1100,
    "w": 700,
    "h": 60
   },
   {
    "id": "a3",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "Apollo 11 powered descent, PDI to touchdown: braking (P63) and approach (P64) on Apollo's quadratic guidance, the landing phase (P66) on a pilot model built from Aldrin's callouts; the descent engine's throttle logic (trim, fixed throttle position, throttle recovery at 57 %); RCS attitude control; touchdown on four footpads.",
    "x": 40,
    "y": -40,
    "w": 960,
    "h": 60
   }
  ]
 },
